From: Isaiah <isaiahdw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dts: rk3576-rock-4d: Nerves fixups (SD as mmcblk0, watchdog)

Two board-dts changes needed by the Nerves system:

1. rk3576-linux.dtsi pins mmc0 = &sdhci and mmc1 = &sdmmc, and the
   vendor kernel derives the mmcblk index from these aliases — so the
   SD card is /dev/mmcblk1 even though the sdhci/eMMC is disabled on
   this board (unusable on SPI-NOR SKUs). Every Nerves reference
   (fw_env.config, erlinit mounts, fwup devpaths) expects the system
   disk at /dev/mmcblk0. Re-point mmc0 at sdmmc and delete the mmc1
   alias; verified on hardware where the mismatch broke the env read,
   the /mnt/boot and /root mounts, and firmware validation.

2. The wdt node is status = "disabled" in rk3576.dtsi and nothing
   enables it. Nerves arms the hardware watchdog through Erlang's
   heart (nerves_heart on /dev/watchdog0 with WATCHDOG_NOWAYOUT).

With UFS boot only the watchdog change (2) is needed; the mmc0 alias
change (1) is legacy from SD boot and harmless.

Applies to both rk3576-rock-4d and rk3576-rock-4d-spi (the -spi dts
includes this file).

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-rock-4d.dts
@@ -745,3 +745,14 @@
 		"", "", "", "";
 };

+
+/ {
+	aliases {
+		mmc0 = &sdmmc;
+		/delete-property/ mmc1;
+	};
+};
+
+&wdt {
+	status = "okay";
+};
